list
[{'id': 'P0001', 'report': 'A', 'text': 'The required build and tests pass, but focused checks found failures in ordinary boundary cases and several ownership errors. There are findings: 6 High, 11 Medium and 4 Low**. No production Rust source was edited; regression harnesses and logs are under `/work/tmp`.\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0002', 'report': 'A', 'text': 'All source locations below are relative to `/work/crate`.\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0003', 'report': 'A', 'text': 'High\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0004', 'report': 'A', 'text': 'Empty collections create invalid slices and abort\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0005', 'report': 'A', 'text': '`src/buf.rs:47`, `src/buf.rs:53`, `src/remote.rs:387`, `src/diff.rs:1281`.\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0006', 'report': 'A', 'text': 'Empty buffers, reference lists and binary data should be readable as empty slices. These methods pass null pointers to `slice::from_raw_parts` or `from_raw_parts_mut`, which require non-null pointers even at length zero.\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0007', 'report': 'A', 'text': 'Executed tests independently produced SIGABRT for:\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0008', 'report': 'A', 'text': '- `Buf::new().is_empty()`.\n- Mutably borrowing a new `Buf`.\n- Listing references from an empty bare remote.\n- Reading binary data from a valid `Binary files … differ` patch marker.\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0009', 'report': 'A', 'text': 'Return empty slices when the length is zero. Existing tests miss these empty-result paths.\n\n'}, {'id': 'P0010', 'report': 'A', 'text': 'Signatures of edited blame lines 
